From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32, kernelbase: Access check result lists, checks with audits, inheritance sources (6057)

The rest of the SEC-ACL and SEC-AUDIT subsets DECISIONS-2 approves.
AccessCheckByTypeResultList and the access checks that audit
(AccessCheckByTypeAndAuditAlarm, AccessCheckByTypeResultListAndAuditAlarm
and its ByHandle form, A and W) were missing, and
AccessCheckAndAuditAlarmW/A were stubs that returned TRUE without a
result. GetInheritanceSourceA/W, FreeInheritedFromArray,
TreeResetNamedSecurityInfoA, TreeSetNamedSecurityInfoA, the impersonate
trustee builders and GetMultipleTrustee(Operation)A/W were missing.

A result list gives each object type its own result: an object ACE for a
type reaches its subtree, a deny for a child does not reach its parent.
The audited checks need SeAuditPrivilege in the caller's primary token
(AUDIT_ALLOW_NO_PRIVILEGE checks without it), check the impersonated
client (or the token given) and generate no audit. GetInheritanceSource
walks up the object's ancestors to the one whose inheritable ACE is its
own. The declarations, AUDIT_EVENT_TYPE and FN_OBJECT_MGR_FUNCTS are
added to the headers.
---
